page('Bug triage: distinguish defects from design concerns')
table([['Case','Current evidence and closure requirement'],['N01 — preview obstruction','Visible in the retained v69 home frame. Reproduce with the signed build, preserve a full-screen recording, then verify the requested floating button no longer masks readable content.'],['N09 — misleading empty state','Source-supported candidate. Populate a disposable library, apply a nonempty zero-match label filter and record the actual empty-state wording.'],['N07 — query scope broadening','Source-supported current contract. First decide and disclose the intended global/local semantics; a deliberate global search is not itself a defect.'],['E01 — context squeezed','Visible usability constraint. Measure readable context with the same IME/font/device before claiming a quantitative improvement.'],['Remaining visual/IA findings','Triage as usability work or hypotheses, not a fabricated count of crashes. Prioritise using observed frequency and severity from real tasks.'],['User-reported bugs','Keep the report open pending device/build, steps, expected/actual result, screen recording and opt-in diagnostics. Do not close as cannot reproduce solely because automation passed.']])
sub('Safety boundary')
para('Any reproduction uses disposable local notes with recorded originals. Do not uninstall, clear app data, replace the signed package or overwrite a user library to simplify testing. Failure injection belongs in a separate disposable environment. Keep diagnostic collection opt-in and never upload private notes or audio.')
page('Proper hands-on comparison: preparation and controls')
para('This is the next testing protocol, not a list of tests claimed to have run. An operator should execute and observe the same user tasks, without following developer-only shortcuts. Capture decisions, confusion, corrections and recovery, not merely a terminal pass line.')
for label,text in [('Matched setup','Use the same physical Android device where possible; otherwise match OS, resolution, density, refresh rate, font scale, IME and thermal/battery conditions. Preserve signing/data safety for our installed app. Record exact builds and source evidence versions.'),('Matched data','Create a public dummy corpus with 50 notes, five folders, three labels/tags, mixed short/long titles and repeated body phrases. Use equivalent content and user outcomes, not identical internal file formats. Add 200-item and long-note variants only for the scale tasks.'),('Counterbalanced order','Alternate which app is used first to reduce learning effects. Separate cold and warm runs. Record novice familiarity and avoid coaching one app more than the other.'),('Observation','Capture screen/touch recordings where consented, operator notes and available frame traces. Ask what the user expects before revealing the result. Keep errors, abandoned attempts and backtracking.'),('Outcome','Verify that the intended note opens, edits persist, original content is retained, and navigation returns to a comprehensible state. Record unknowns instead of assigning a zero.')]:block(label,text)
page('Hands-on task sheet A: retrieval and organisation — NOT RUN')
tasks=[('T01','Retrieve a remembered title','From home, find a specified note among 50 mixed items without naming its creation workspace. Verify its ID/content. Record task time, navigation switches, wrong opens and help requests.'),('T02','Body-only phrase with a filter','Apply a folder/label filter, search a phrase found only in note bodies, and explain the visible scope before opening the result. Verify the expected IDs under the app’s stated contract.'),('T03','Create a folder during a move','Move one dummy item into a newly named folder. Repeat Cancel, invalid name and Back branches. Verify original content, selected destination and return context.'),('T04','Recover from an apparently empty list','Use a filter that returns zero items while the library remains populated. Determine why the view is empty and restore visibility without recreating notes or clearing storage.')]
for id,title,text in tasks:sub(id+' | '+title);para(text)
para('Status: all four tasks are planned, not executed in this report. An instruction-path count would not be a measured task outcome.','SmallUX')
page('Hands-on task sheet B: editing and reading — NOT RUN')
for id,title,text in [('T05','Format in context','Write 250 words, select a middle phrase, apply bold and a heading, then resume typing. Record visible context, selection errors, unintended formatting, panel reopenings and saved result.'),('T06','Navigate a long note','Find a named section among twenty headings and repeated words, edit it, then return to the previous location. Use each app’s best discoverable method; do not require a feature name.'),('T07','Read and modify a mixed note','Read a paragraph, a checklist and a table; change one row and move one block if that operation is supported. Separate unavailable outcomes from failures. Verify unrelated content is unchanged.'),('T08','Save and interruption confidence','Save, navigate away and reopen the same dummy note. In an isolated failure-injection environment, trigger a controlled save failure and observe feedback/retry. Never apply destructive testing to a real library.')]:sub(id+' | '+title);para(text)
para('Run at standard and enlarged font scales. A screenshot of a retained selection is not proof of smooth dragging or a comfortable writing session.','SmallUX')
page('Smoothness, latency and effectiveness: measurement ledger')
table([['Measure','Protocol / present result'],['Tap to usable response','Timestamp the input and first stable usable state in recorded evidence. Separate keyboard appearance and app rendering. Present result: NOT MEASURED.'],['Scroll and drag quality','Capture frame traces and user-visible recordings for list scrolling, note scrolling, selection drag and reordering. State refresh rate and trace-derived jank definition. Present result: NOT MEASURED.'],['Cold / warm startup','Record process/cache state and time to usable content, not just launch intent dispatch. Present result: NOT MEASURED head-to-head.'],['Task efficiency','Time, action count, wrong turns, corrections and abandonments on the matched tasks. Present result: NOT MEASURED.'],['Task effectiveness','Correct item, correct scope, intended edit and saved content verified after reopen. Present result: NOT MEASURED on a matched manual task set.'],['Confidence / perceived simplicity','Ask users what is happening, where they are and whether work is safe; record the explanation and uncertainty. Present result: no participant study.'],['Resource use','Installed storage, data/cache growth, peak working memory and battery under equivalent tasks. APK payload alone is not any of these. Present result: NOT MEASURED.']])
para('Do not substitute OCR/speech benchmark timings, native test counts, JPEG file sizes or API callback success for these metrics. No claim that a fast automated call means a smooth human interaction.')
page('Acceptance gates before calling a module polished')
for label,text in [('Readability','No primary floating action masks required text in the evaluated state; no clipped essential scope/status wording; important content remains available with keyboard and large text.'),('Predictability','Search scope and active filters are understandable; first-use empty and filtered-empty are distinct; each action’s object and return destination are clear.'),('Effectiveness','Users reach and modify the intended content without developer assistance. Saved content matches their intent after reopen, including mixed formatting and structured blocks.'),('Efficiency','Measured task results show fewer unnecessary transitions or less scanning; retain negative and neutral outcomes. No improvement claim before comparable measurements exist.'),('Smoothness','Live traces/recordings show acceptable task-specific feedback and no disruptive interaction stalls under declared conditions. Define thresholds before testing, not after seeing the result.'),('Safety and recovery','No data loss, unsafe Back navigation or silent replacement. Preserve originals and clear failure feedback; verify install-over rather than destructive reset when needed.')]:block(label,text)
page('What to preserve; what not to copy blindly')
para('Our plain title/body editor and labelled Insert / Format / Voice / Background actions are already understandable in M07/M08. Existing global cross-workspace search, folder/label controls, grid/list choice, highlighted find return and shared FormatControls should be improved, not described as nonexistent.')
para('Obsidian’s useful references here are focused retrieval/action surfaces, a visible heading outline, calmer rendered prose and compact keyboard-adjacent actions. Its unlabelled icons, Markdown concepts, substantial frontmatter and distributed navigation can themselves confuse beginners. Its font-size settings also expose pixels; it is not an automatic model of plain-language typography.')
para('Preserve our requested floating New note, single A Format entry, fifth inline Clear action, compact editor header, safe Back behaviour, direct editing, long-selection persistence and accessible per-content actions. Proposed directions are design hypotheses, not authorisation to undo earlier requirements.')
para('No extra-feature credit is awarded for our voice/OCR/drawing tools, nor is missing a third-party plugin counted as a failure in this shared-task review. A simple app should not become a complicated clone of the comparator.')
page('Next modules and work boundary')
table([['Stage','Scope and evidence needed'],['This installment','Two modules only: find/organise and edit/read. Twenty scoped findings and a proposed matched manual task set. No fixes or new Android builds.'],['Next: file viewers','Compare opening, navigation, selection, search, zoom, copy/export and return paths for shared file types. Use original documents and actual interactions, not only viewer launch captures.'],['Next: tables / lists / rich content depth','Evaluate cell/row edits, context actions, ordering and data retention as user workflows. Avoid a feature-count table that treats presence as usability.'],['Next: navigation / settings / recovery','Review onboarding, storage explanations, archive/trash, saving failures and recovery with disposable data. Retain signing/data safety.'],['Separate specialised modules','OCR, speech, drawings and other non-equivalent capabilities need their own effectiveness tests or suitable comparators, not invented Obsidian counterparts.'],['Implementation later','Convert validated findings into small changes, retain regression safeguards, then repeat the same manual acceptance tasks. User approval of this review is not evidence that a fix is complete.']])
page('Evidence catalogue and reproduction references')
para('Source frames are retained in the repository; the evidence manifest stores exact paths, SHA-256 digests and dimensions. These are historical captures, not new screenshots from this review. Source images are not duplicated into this report folder.')
